---
description: LAN Sentinel project rules; read AGENTS.md first
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` at the repository root before changing anything. It holds the hard rules (§4), the source-of-truth order (§2), the package map, what to run (§8) and the common tasks (§10). This rule only restates what must never be missed.

- Linux-only, static `CGO_ENABLED=0` Go; never add a cgo dependency.
- Run Go only through `make` (Linux dev container); `make check` is the gate.
- Collectors and probes only emit observations; only `internal/correlate` mutates state and writes events; one SQLite writer.
- A host is one MAC per interface (UUID `host_id`); never merge or split.
- Kernel access only in `internal/platform`.
- OT safety rules 7, 11 and 12 are not negotiable without a recorded decision.
- If code and docs disagree, or a decision is missing, ask.
